WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:06.000
Wonder Woman 1984 is packed with surprises,&nbsp;
action and emotion. There's a lot going on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.520
in this neon fairy tale, so you might&nbsp;
not catch it all on your first viewing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:12.800
Here's the full story, including&nbsp;
the key elements of the ending.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.920
Obviously, spoilers are ahead. You've been warned!

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:22.240
Some 70 years after the events of the first&nbsp;
Wonder Woman, Diana lives in a luxurious condo in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:28.080
Washington, D.C. She chooses to spend time alone&nbsp;
after losing her one true love, Steve Trevor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:33.120
in World War I. Her home is decorated with&nbsp;
pictures of Steve, and Diana chooses to eat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:37.680
dinner by herself and avoid human connection&nbsp;
while working at the Smithsonian by day.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:42.160
"Diana, look at you. It's&nbsp;
like not one day has passed."

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:46.800
But Diana still dons her armor and stands up&nbsp;
for what's right, even if it's only by going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:52.560
after small-time crooks. During a robbery at&nbsp;
a D.C. mall, four would-be artifact thieves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:57.680
are mystified when a stunning woman clad in red,&nbsp;
blue, and gold swings from the ceiling with her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:03.760
golden Lasso of Truth, dumping them onto a police&nbsp;
cruiser before vanishing. However, she does allow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:09.120
one person a few glimpses — a little girl who&nbsp;
watches Diana vanquish the robbers in adoration,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:13.600
with Diana giving the girl a quick wink before&nbsp;
disappearing to keep her identity a secret.

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:18.320
Diana might prefer to be alone, but she&nbsp;
ends up making a friend when the meek,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:23.120
awkward Barbara Minerva joins the&nbsp;
Smithsonian staff as a gemologist.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:27.840
Constantly tripping over her own feet and&nbsp;
too soft-spoken to stand up for herself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:33.520
Barbara immediately idealizes everything about&nbsp;
Diana, who comes off as strong and confident.

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:38.960
After Barbara shows Diana some of the artifacts&nbsp;
she's studying, including a mysterious citrine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:44.400
stone, Diana agrees to go out for a drink after&nbsp;
work. The two end up bonding, with Diana praising&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:49.120
Barbara's sweet personality and open nature,&nbsp;
admitting that she prefers to close herself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:54.800
off from the world. Later that evening, alone&nbsp;
in a park, Barbara is assaulted by a drunk man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.800 --> 00:02:00.880
but Diana comes to her rescue. Rather than raising&nbsp;
questions about Diana's apparent super-strength,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:04.640
the incident only makes Barbara&nbsp;
aspire to be like Diana even more.

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:10.800
Down-on-his-luck would-be oil tycoon Maxwell&nbsp;
Lord first appears on television screens in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:15.760
mall where Diana stops the robbery, as he tries&nbsp;
to convince folks that they can improve their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:21.280
lives with the help of his company, Black Gold&nbsp;
Cooperative. Despite the glossy feel of his ads,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:26.160
Maxwell is broke, and his top investor,&nbsp;
Simon Stagg, is getting angry.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:31.760
Desperate to make money — and support as&nbsp;
well as impress his young son Alistair,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:37.920
Maxwell seeks out a rather unorthodox fix. When&nbsp;
he hears about the stone that Barbara and Diana&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:43.440
have discovered, the Dreamstone, he sees a way out&nbsp;
of his predicament. He comes up with a plan to use&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:49.828
the Dreamstone for his own gains, seducing Barbara&nbsp;
to gain access to the artifact for himself.

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:54.640
Before Max takes possession of the stone,&nbsp;
both Diana and Barbara wish upon it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:57.360
though neither of them quite&nbsp;
understand what they're doing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:02.880
Diana wishes that Steve could still be with her.&nbsp;
The next day, at a Smithsonian gala, she's taken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:08.320
aback when she discovers that Steve, living&nbsp;
in someone else's body, has indeed returned.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:12.720
Meanwhile, Barbara wishes for the confidence&nbsp;
and power of her new friend Diana,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:18.080
and begins to see a change almost immediately.&nbsp;
She's suddenly striding around the Smithsonian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:21.760
in slinky outfits and attracting&nbsp;
attention from everyone around her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:27.360
At a Gala, Maxwell invites her into a room alone,&nbsp;
but it's all a ruse to steal the Dreamstone.

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:32.320
Maxwell takes his wish a huge step&nbsp;
further, too, becoming the stone himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:36.960
so he can grant anybody's wishes as well&nbsp;
as his own. With this power, Maxwell can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:42.560
manipulate the entire world, making deals with&nbsp;
international figures and causing complete chaos.

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:48.240
All three wishers eventually realize&nbsp;
there's a huge downside to the Dreamstone:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:53.360
it steals your life essence when you make a wish.&nbsp;
Diana might be happy with Steve by her side,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:58.720
but her powers are fading. She's unable to harness&nbsp;
her strength or properly wield the Lasso of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:03.760
Truth. Barbara completely loses the humanity&nbsp;
that drew Diana to her in the first place,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:07.200
driven only by vengeance and a thirst&nbsp;
for more strength and influence.

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:11.040
“You've always had everything, while&nbsp;
people like me have had nothing."

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:14.080
To make matters worse, Barbara&nbsp;
makes more wishes on the stone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:19.120
through Maxwell, turning herself into&nbsp;
the animalistic, hyper-strong Cheetah.

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:24.160
Maxwell fares worst of all. As he continues&nbsp;
to grant wishes and emotionally manipulate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:28.880
the world so he has power over everybody,&nbsp;
even the president of the United States,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:34.160
his body begins to break down. His nose&nbsp;
and ears stream blood, his eyes are red.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:39.600
His body is visibly wrecked. Despite these&nbsp;
negative effects, everyone, even Diana,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:44.320
is loath to let go of their wishes, even when&nbsp;
they discover that the stone was created by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:49.520
the God of Treachery and Mischief himself. But&nbsp;
the only way to return to normal is to recant.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:55.120
Diana and Steve realize there's only one thing&nbsp;
she can do to regain her power and bring down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:59.760
Maxwell and Barbara: recant her wish.&nbsp;
After yet another emotional goodbye,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:05.200
a sobbing Diana takes her wish back, and Steve&nbsp;
shuffles off this mortal coil once again.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:10.000
With her full powers returned, Diana&nbsp;
discovers Maxwell's plan to use a U.S.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:15.120
military broadcast system to speak to the&nbsp;
entire world so he can grant wishes en masse.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:20.160
Diana, in the full splendor of the&nbsp;
ancient golden Amazonian armor of Asteria,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:26.080
defeats Cheetah, electrocuting her to turn her&nbsp;
back into Barbara. She then confronts Maxwell.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:31.520
She wraps the Lasso of Truth around him and speaks&nbsp;
to the world over the broadcast system, begging&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:38.160
everyone to recant their wishes. The do, stopping&nbsp;
a nuclear war as a result. Diana also uses the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:44.000
Lasso to show Maxwell a vision of his young son&nbsp;
Alistair, convincing him to return to his family.

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:49.920
At the beginning of the movie, a much younger&nbsp;
Diana competes in a hyper-athletic sporting event.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:54.160
Though she's the youngest competitor&nbsp;
by far, Diana immediately takes first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:58.880
place — but when she's knocked off her&nbsp;
horse at a crucial moment, all seems lost.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:03.440
But Diana finds a secret shortcut,&nbsp;
putting her firmly back in first place.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:07.760
When she returns to the arena, her aunt&nbsp;
Antiope disqualifies her, saying she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:13.520
cheated. Diana protests, but Antiope tells her&nbsp;
that victory can't be achieved by dishonesty,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:19.600
stressing that truth is of the utmost importance.&nbsp;
She tells Diana, "No true hero is born from lies."

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:22.880
"And remember, greatness is not what you think."

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:27.920
Diana is disappointed in the moment, but she takes&nbsp;
those lessons about truth and honesty with her.

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:33.360
Antiope's message of honesty proves especially&nbsp;
important by the end of Wonder Woman 1984.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:36.320
Through all three characters&nbsp;
and their Dreamstone wishes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:41.360
it's clear Diana, Barbara, and Maxwell are&nbsp;
all pretending to be somebody they're not.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:46.480
The Stone exposes their greatest flaws,&nbsp;
even as it gives them their hearts' desire.

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:51.360
Though it seems to people like Barbara that&nbsp;
Diana has zero problems in her perfect life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:56.160
Diana's unwillingness to engage with anybody&nbsp;
in the wake of losing Steve is a front for her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.160 --> 00:07:01.360
loneliness and a craving for human connection.&nbsp;
Barbara, rather than finding confidence within&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:07.200
herself, tries to steal Diana's. Meanwhile,&nbsp;
Maxwell wants to appear powerful at any cost,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:11.920
despite the fact that he's broke and his business&nbsp;
is failing. In the end, whether they're giving up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:17.040
true love, finding their own confidence,&nbsp;
or reuniting with family, Diana, Barbara,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:22.960
and Maxwell understand that the Stone, despite its&nbsp;
seductive wish-granting abilities, can't actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:28.480
help them at all. Only honesty and clarity can&nbsp;
lead to true greatness. You can't take shortcuts.

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:34.400
In the aftermath of Maxwell's hostile&nbsp;
takeover and a narrowly averted nuclear war,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:37.760
the world seems to return to&nbsp;
normal by the holiday season.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:42.320
Back in D.C. and alone once more, Diana&nbsp;
watches families spend time together at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:46.720
a Christmas village, and even without&nbsp;
Steve in her life, she seems at peace.

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:52.400
However, the clearest example of Diana's personal&nbsp;
progress comes when she finds herself face to face&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:58.320
with the man whose body Steve inhabited during his&nbsp;
recent turn on Earth. Rather than closing herself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:03.760
off, Diana lets herself open up to this stranger,&nbsp;
complimenting the outfit we saw Steve try on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:08.720
earlier and giving him a warm smile before they&nbsp;
part ways. Whether they'll meet again isn't clear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.720 --> 00:08:13.920
but what's important is that Diana, who was once&nbsp;
so committed to being alone, is willing to make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:19.360
human connections once again, letting Steve go&nbsp;
once and for all and living life on her own terms.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:24.800
She also harnesses some impressive superpowers,&nbsp;
mastering flying through the clouds with ease.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:28.640
In the aftermath of her experience with&nbsp;
the Stone, she's even more powerful.

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:35.520
Throughout the film, the audience and Diana learn&nbsp;
about Asteria, an ancient Amazonian who sacrificed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.520 --> 00:08:41.120
herself and her strength to protect Themyscira&nbsp;
from the prying eyes of men. During the flashback&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:46.560
to Diana's childhood, her mother, Queen Hippolyta,&nbsp;
soothes her distraught daughter by showing her the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:51.600
golden statue of Asteria and telling the story&nbsp;
of the brave warrior who saved the island.

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:54.640
When the audience gets a brief&nbsp;
glimpse of Asteria herself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:59.600
the actor playing her looks familiar. And for&nbsp;
good reason, as she's played by Lynda Carter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:04.720
who played Wonder Woman on the small screen&nbsp;
in the 1970s. In a post-credits sequence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.720 --> 00:09:10.560
it's revealed that Asteria, like Diana, secretly&nbsp;
lives among humankind. Whether Carter appears in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:15.520
a future Wonder Woman installment remains to be&nbsp;
seen, but no matter what, it's fascinating to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:20.480
learn that Diana isn't alone, and potentially&nbsp;
has an incredibly powerful ally nearby.

